{
    "background_story": "Neriah was a brilliant and adventurous travel writer, but a debilitating illness had left her unable to explore the world as she once did. Undeterred, she found a new way to experience the thrill of discovery through others. She began to live vicariously through her niece, Ava, who was a fearless globe-trotter. Neriah would pour over Ava's stories, photos, and videos, feeling as though she was right there with her, hiking through the Himalayas or island-hopping in Greece. As Ava's travels took her to more and more exotic destinations, Neriah's writing flourished, inspired by the second-hand experiences. Her readers devoured her vivid descriptions, none the wiser that the true adventurer was not Neriah herself, but her intrepid niece. Through Ava's eyes, Neriah continued to explore the world, her imagination and creativity fueled by the thrill of vicarious adventure.",
